{
  "slug": "windows-11-wifi-keeps-disconnecting",
  "title": "Why Windows 11 Keeps Disconnecting Wi-Fi, and How to Fix It",
  "description": "Windows 11 Wi-Fi keeps disconnecting every few minutes? Try these 9 fixes, from a driver setting to a full network reset.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "PC Maintenance",
    "Troubleshooting",
    "Networking"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/windows-11-wifi-keeps-disconnecting/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 930,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "Why Windows 11 Keeps Disconnecting Wi-Fi, and How to Fix It",
      "subtitle": "Windows 11 Wi-Fi keeps disconnecting every few minutes? Try these 9 fixes, from a driver…",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Save your open work. Save the name and the password of your Wi-Fi network. Connect a phone to the same network.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Run the Network Troubleshooter",
      "body": "Windows 11 has a troubleshooter that repairs common network errors. The Get Help app contains a second troubleshooter. Open Settings.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Restart the Router and the Computer",
      "body": "A router that runs for weeks can stop a stable connection. A restart clears its memory. Disconnect the power from the router. Wait 30 seconds.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Forget the Network and Connect Again",
      "body": "Windows stores the password and the security type of every network. A wrong stored password stops the connection.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Stop the Adapter Power Saving",
      "body": "Windows turns off the wireless adapter to save power. This turn off breaks the connection after a few minutes. This fault causes most of the drops.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Set One Wireless Band",
      "body": "Some routers use the same name for the 2.4 GHz band and the 5 GHz band. An adapter with automatic band selection can then lose the connection.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
